S3_BUCKET=production-us-west-2-outreach-web
CF_DISTRIBUTION_ID=E1HAHSEJI5YNWC
ASSUME_ROLE=arn:aws:iam::792513288588:role/github-actions-deploy

# Both values come from the site's own unit, which lives in the separate
# `infrastructure` checkout (a sibling of this repo — there is no `infrastructure/`
# path inside the monorepo):
#
#   cd <infrastructure>/environments/production/us-west-2/static-sites/outreach-web
#   terragrunt output -raw s3_bucket_id
#   terragrunt output -raw cloudfront_distribution_id
#
# Applied 2026-10-09 in account 792513288588 (AdministratorAccess-Production):
# 11 resources added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed. CF_DISTRIBUTION_ID is assigned by
# AWS at creation, so unlike S3_BUCKET it cannot be written in advance — re-read
# it if the distribution is ever replaced.
#
# S3_BUCKET and ASSUME_ROLE match the sibling apps — same naming scheme, same
# per-environment deploy role — so nothing new has to be created for outreach.
#
# The distribution carries `outreach.betterangels.la` as an alias and is served
# on `outreach.prod.betterangels.la`, both covered by the shared
# `*.betterangels.la` / `*.prod.betterangels.la` certificate.
